From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tau <noreply@tau.new>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:04:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] core: read clocks through a wasm-safe time module

On wasm32-unknown-unknown std::time::Instant::now() and
SystemTime::now() panic: the target has no clock. The Fusion history
observers time their passes and the IGES writer stamps the file with
the current time, so a conversion that reaches either panics in the
browser. Add cadmpeg_core::time with Stopwatch, whose elapsed time is
zero where no clock exists, and system_now(), which returns the Unix
epoch there, and route the three call sites through it. Native
behaviour is unchanged.
